# Context exclusions for contest-scout/Dockerfile.
#
# This file rather than a repo-root .dockerignore: the build context has to be
# the repo root (the image bakes in .claude/skills/find-contests), but the rest
# of the repo — the portfolio UI, the store, 400MB of git history — has nothing
# to do with this image. BuildKit reads <dockerfile>.dockerignore in preference
# to the context's, so these rules stay scoped to this one build.
#
# Deny everything, then allow exactly what the Dockerfile COPYs. An allowlist
# means a new directory elsewhere in the repo can never quietly join the
# context, and nothing outside these three paths can end up in a layer.
*
!contest-scout/scripts
!contest-scout/config/contest-deadlines.md
!.claude/skills/find-contests

# Never shipped even from the allowed paths: bytecode is arch-specific and
# credentials are not built into images (config comes from the environment).
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.env
